<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Talk on Vlad Temian - Centrist Tech Optimist</title><link>https://blog.vtemian.com/tags/talk/</link><description>Recent content in Talk on Vlad Temian - Centrist Tech Optimist</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.vtemian.com/tags/talk/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>The One-Person Product Team</title><link>https://blog.vtemian.com/talk/the-one-person-product-team/</link><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://blog.vtemian.com/talk/the-one-person-product-team/</guid><description>&lt;p>On the morning of my talk, &lt;a href="https://sisif.ai">sisif.ai&lt;/a> was &lt;em>losing customers&lt;/em> and I didn&amp;rsquo;t know why. I sent one message, typos included, to the Grok Bot agent I call &lt;span class="agent-chip" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.35em;height:1.55em;padding:0 0.65em 0 0.13em;margin:0 0.1em;border-radius:999px;background:#1c1c1e;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.14);color:#f2f2f2;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1;vertical-align:-0.35em;white-space:nowrap;">&lt;img src="https://blog.vtemian.com/talk/the-one-person-product-team/avatar-boss.png" alt="" style="display:block;width:1.3em;height:1.3em;max-width:none;margin:0;border-radius:50%;box-shadow:none;">boss&lt;/span>: &amp;ldquo;boss, we need something! &amp;hellip; we&amp;rsquo;re loosing customers. check in posthog and stripe.&amp;ldquo;&lt;span class="anno">&lt;label for="sn-4af4a15da3" class="anno-mark" tabindex="0">&lt;/label>&lt;input type="checkbox" id="sn-4af4a15da3" class="anno-toggle">&lt;span class="sidenote">&lt;span class="sidenote-inner">My agents have job titles. &lt;span class="agent-chip" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.35em;height:1.55em;padding:0 0.65em 0 0.13em;margin:0 0.1em;border-radius:999px;background:#1c1c1e;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.14);color:#f2f2f2;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1;vertical-align:-0.35em;white-space:nowrap;">&lt;img src="https://blog.vtemian.com/talk/the-one-person-product-team/avatar-boss.png" alt="" style="display:block;width:1.3em;height:1.3em;max-width:none;margin:0;border-radius:50%;box-shadow:none;">boss&lt;/span> coordinates and talks to me, &lt;span class="agent-chip" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.35em;height:1.55em;padding:0 0.65em 0 0.13em;margin:0 0.1em;border-radius:999px;background:#1c1c1e;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.14);color:#f2f2f2;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1;vertical-align:-0.35em;white-space:nowrap;">&lt;img src="https://blog.vtemian.com/talk/the-one-person-product-team/avatar-kitchen.png" alt="" style="display:block;width:1.3em;height:1.3em;max-width:none;margin:0;border-radius:50%;box-shadow:none;">kitchen&lt;/span> writes and ships code, &lt;span class="agent-chip" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.35em;height:1.55em;padding:0 0.65em 0 0.13em;margin:0 0.1em;border-radius:999px;background:#1c1c1e;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.14);color:#f2f2f2;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1;vertical-align:-0.35em;white-space:nowrap;">&lt;img src="https://blog.vtemian.com/talk/the-one-person-product-team/avatar-qa.png" alt="" style="display:block;width:1.3em;height:1.3em;max-width:none;margin:0;border-radius:50%;box-shadow:none;">qa&lt;/span> clicks through production like a user would. Next to them sit marketing, seo and commerce, which works on the Shopify app, and plenty of other bots.&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Why I Think Software Development Will Be Automated by 2030</title><link>https://blog.vtemian.com/talk/why-i-think-software-development-will-be-automated-by-2030/</link><pubDate>Fri, 27 Mar 2026 10:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://blog.vtemian.com/talk/why-i-think-software-development-will-be-automated-by-2030/</guid><description>&lt;p>&lt;img src="debate-1.jpeg" alt="Debating at All-Stack Hangout">&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Last night I debated &amp;ldquo;Will AI fully automate the Software Development Life Cycle by 2030?&amp;rdquo; at &lt;a href="https://luma.com/hl1u9s3a">All-Stack Hangout&lt;/a> in Timisoara, organized by &lt;a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/victorysquarepartners/">Victory Square Partners&lt;/a>. I was on the PRO side, alongside &lt;a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alexbinzar/">Alexandru Binzar&lt;/a> (CEO, Hibyte). Against us: &lt;a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tomacristian/">Cristian Toma&lt;/a> (20-year software engineer) and &lt;a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/marius-balaj/">Marius Balaj&lt;/a> (UI engineer turned founder). &lt;a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/laviniacioloca/">Lavinia Cioloca&lt;/a> moderated.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>What started as a structured debate turned into a real conversation. This post is my case, expanded and fact-checked.&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>